affineToricRing -- computes the toric ring associated to a monomial map
***********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        affineToricRing L
        affineToricRing M
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of lists; each list corresponds
        to a vector in $\mathbb Z^n$
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, with each column
        corresponding to a vector in $\mathbb Z^n$
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, 

Description
===========

Given a list $\{v_1,...,v_d\}$ of vectors in $\mathbb Z^n$ this function
computes the toric ring $R/I$ where $R$ is the polynomial ring
$\mathbb{Q}[x_1,\dots,x_d]$ with $x_i$ having degree $v_i$ and $I$ is the
associated toric ideal. In particular $I$ is the kernel of the map $R \to
\mathbb{Q}[y_1,\dots,y_n]$ defined by $x_i \mapsto \mathbb y^{v_i}$.

+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : L = {{2,0},{1,1},{0,2}};                             |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : X = affineToricRing L; -- The singular quadric in A^3|
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : I = ideal X                                          |
|                                                          |
|            2                                             |
|o3 = ideal(x  - x x )                                     |
|            1    0 2                                      |
|                                                          |
|o3 : Ideal of QQ[x ..x ]                                  |
|                  0   2                                   |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : hilbertSeries I                                      |
|                                                          |
|                   2 2                                    |
|              1 - T T                                     |
|                   0 1                                    |
|o4 = --------------------------                           |
|           2                 2                            |
|     (1 - T )(1 - T T )(1 - T )                           |
|           1       0 1       0                            |
|                                                          |
|o4 : Expression of class Divide                           |
+----------------------------------------------------------+

