ampleKClass -- the class of an ample line bundle
************************************************

  * Usage: 
        ampleKClass(X)
  * Inputs:
      * X, a *note GKM variety: GKMVariety,, 
      * C, an *note equivariant K-class: KClass,, 
  * Outputs:
      * an *note equivariant K-class: KClass,, 

Description
===========

If $X$ is a GKM variety with a distinguished ample equivariant line bundle,
this method returns the *note KClass: KClass, of the line bundle. If no such
line bundle is defined, it allows the user to construct one.

The following example describes the ample line bundle on the Lagrangian
Grassmannian $SpGr(2,4)$. The line bundle is precisely the pullback of O(1)
under the Plücker embedding $SpGr(2,4) \to \mathbb P^4$.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : SpGr24 = generalizedFlagVariety("C",2,{2})                              |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = a "GKM variety" with an action of a 2-dimensional torus                 |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : GKMVariety                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : O1 = ampleKClass SpGr24                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = an "equivariant K-class" on a GKM variety                               |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : KClass                                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : peek O1                                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = KClass{variety => a "GKM variety" with an action of a 2-dimensional     |
|                                                          -1                 |
|            KPolynomials => HashTable{{set {0, 1*}} => T T    }              |
|                                                        0 1                  |
|                                      {set {0, 1}} => T T                    |
|                                                       0 1                   |
|                                                         -1 -1               |
|                                      {set {1*, 0*}} => T  T                 |
|                                                         0  1                |
|                                                        -1                   |
|                                      {set {1, 0*}} => T  T                  |
|                                                        0  1                 |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|torus}                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

