EquivariantMap -- the class of all equivariant morphisms between GKM varieties
******************************************************************************

Description
===========

Given two GKM varieties $X$ and $Y$, an equivariant morphism from $X$ to $Y$
induces a map from the torus-fixed points of $X$ to the torus-fixed points of
$Y$.



A *note EquivariantMap: EquivariantMap, C is a *note HashTable:
(Macaulay2Doc)HashTable, consisting of three keys:

  * source, whose value is a *note GKMVariety: GKMVariety, corresponding to the
    domain of f
  * target, whose value is a *note GKMVariety: GKMVariety, corresponding to the
    codomain of f
  * ptsMap, whose value is a *note HashTable: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,; its
    keys are X.points and the values are points of Y.points that the key maps
    to.



See also
========

  * *note EquivariantMap ** EquivariantMap: EquivariantMap _st_st
    EquivariantMap, -- computes the product of two equivariant morphisms
  * *note compose(EquivariantMap,EquivariantMap):
    compose_lpEquivariantMap_cmEquivariantMap_rp, -- computes the composition
    of two equivariant morphisms
  * *note map(GKMVariety,GKMVariety,List):
    map_lpGKMVariety_cmGKMVariety_cmList_rp, -- creates a EquivariantMap
  * *note flagMap: flagMap, -- creates equivariant maps between generalized
    flag varieties
  * *note pullback(EquivariantMap): pullback_lpEquivariantMap_rp, -- computes
    the pullback map of equivariant K-classes of an equivariant map
  * *note pushforward: pushforward, -- computes the pushforward map of
    equivariant K-classes of an equivariant map
  * *note euler(KClass): euler_lpKClass_rp, -- computes the equivariant Euler
    characteristic of an equivariant K-class

Functions and methods returning an equivariant map:
===================================================

  * *note compose(EquivariantMap,EquivariantMap):
    compose_lpEquivariantMap_cmEquivariantMap_rp, -- computes the composition
    of two equivariant morphisms
  * "diagonalMap(GKMVariety)" -- see *note diagonalMap: diagonalMap, --
    constructs the diagonal morphism
  * *note EquivariantMap ** EquivariantMap: EquivariantMap _st_st
    EquivariantMap, -- computes the product of two equivariant morphisms
  * "flagMap(GKMVariety,GKMVariety)" -- see *note flagMap: flagMap, -- creates
    equivariant maps between generalized flag varieties
