euler(KClass) -- computes the equivariant Euler characteristic of an equivariant K-class
****************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note euler: (Macaulay2Doc)euler,
  * Usage: 
        euler C
  * Inputs:
      * C, an *note equivariant K-class: KClass,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, in the character ring
        of the torus of the GKM variety on which C is defined

Description
===========

This method computes the pushforward of a *note KClass: KClass, on a *note
GKMVariety: GKMVariety, $X$ along the structure map $X \to pt$, where $pt$ is a
point with trivial torus-action.



+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : PP3 = projectiveSpace 3                                |
|                                                            |
|o1 = a "GKM variety" with an action of a 4-dimensional torus|
|                                                            |
