FlagMatroid -- the class of all flag matroids
*********************************************

Description
===========

A flag matroid $\mathbf M$ is an ordered list $\{M_1, \ldots, M_k\}$ of *note
Matroid: (Matroids)Matroid,s on a common ground set such that $M_i$ is a
matroid quotient of $M_{i+1}$ for all $i=1, \ldots, k-1$.  The matroids $M_i$'s
are called the "constituent" matroids of the flag matroid $\mathbf M$.  The
class *note FlagMatroid: FlagMatroid, is a *note HashTable:
(Macaulay2Doc)HashTable, with two keys:

  * groundSet, whose value is a *note Set: (Macaulay2Doc)Set, representing the
    common ground set of the constituent matroids
  * constituents, whose value is a *note List: (Macaulay2Doc)List, of *note
    Matroid: (Matroids)Matroid,s



Caveat
======

Flag matroids are the first examples beyond ordinary matroids of a more general
combinatorial family known as Coxeter matroids.  Coxeter matroids have not been
implemented yet.

See also
========

  * *note flagMatroid(List): flagMatroid, -- construct a flag matroid
  * *note flagMatroid(Matrix,List): flagMatroid, -- construct a flag matroid
  * *note makeKClass(GKMVariety,FlagMatroid):
    makeKClass_lpGKMVariety_cmFlagMatroid_rp, -- the equivariant K-class of a
    flag matroid

Functions and methods returning a flag matroid:
===============================================

  * "flagMatroid(List)" -- see *note flagMatroid: flagMatroid, -- construct a
    flag matroid
  * "flagMatroid(Matrix,List)" -- see *note flagMatroid: flagMatroid, --
    construct a flag matroid

Methods that use a flag matroid:
================================

  * *note bases(FlagMatroid): bases_lpFlagMatroid_rp, -- compute the bases of a
    flag matroid
  * "flagGeomTuttePolynomial(FlagMatroid)" -- see *note
    flagGeomTuttePolynomial: flagGeomTuttePolynomial, -- computes the
    flag-geometric Tutte polynomial of flag matroids
  * *note isWellDefined(FlagMatroid): isWellDefined_lpFlagMatroid_rp, -- check
    if a flag matroid is well-defined
  * *note latticePoints(FlagMatroid): latticePoints_lpFlagMatroid_rp, --
    lattice points of a base polytope of a flag matroid
  * *note makeKClass(GKMVariety,FlagMatroid):
    makeKClass_lpGKMVariety_cmFlagMatroid_rp, -- the equivariant K-class of a
    flag matroid

For the programmer
==================

The object *note FlagMatroid: FlagMatroid, is a *note type:
(Macaulay2Doc)Type,, with ancestor classes *note HashTable:
(Macaulay2Doc)HashTable, < *note Thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,.

