flagMatroid -- construct a flag matroid
***************************************

  * Usage: 
        FM = flagMatroid(ML)
        FM = flagMatroid(A,L)
  * Inputs:
      * ML, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of *note Matroid:
        (Matroids)Matroid,s on a common ground set
      * A, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, 
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of integers between 1 and the
        number of rows of A (inclusive)
  * Outputs:
      * FM, a *note flag matroid: FlagMatroid,, 

Description
===========

Given a list $ML$ of matroids on a common ground set, this method stores the
data as a *note FlagMatroid: FlagMatroid,.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : ML = {uniformMatroid(2,6),matroid completeGraph 4}                      |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = {a "matroid" of rank 2 on 6 elements, a "matroid" of rank 3 on 6        |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     elements}                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : FM = flagMatroid(ML)                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = a "flag matroid" with rank sequence {2, 3} on 6 elements                |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : FlagMatroid                                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : isWellDefined FM                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = true                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

For $A$ an $r\times n$ matrix over a field and $L = \{r_1, \ldots, r_k}$ a list
of integers, let $M_i$ be the *note Matroid: (Matroids)Matroid, defined by the
columns of the matrix obtained by the first $r_i$ rows of $A$. These matroids
form a flag matroid $\mathbf M = \{M_1, \ldots, M_k\}$. This method creates
this *note FlagMatroid: FlagMatroid,.

+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : A = random(QQ^2,QQ^4)                                    |
|                                                              |
|o4 = | 9/2 3/4 7/9  7/10 |                                    |
|     | 9/4 7/4 7/10 7/3  |                                    |
|                                                              |
|              2       4                                       |
|o4 : Matrix QQ  <-- QQ                                        |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : FM = flagMatroid(A,{1,2})                                |
|                                                              |
|o5 = a "flag matroid" with rank sequence {1, 2} on 4 elements |
|                                                              |
|o5 : FlagMatroid                                              |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

When a list of matroids is given as input, this method does not check if the
flag matroid is well-defined.

See also
========

  * *note isWellDefined(FlagMatroid): isWellDefined_lpFlagMatroid_rp, -- check
    if a flag matroid is well-defined
  * *note FlagMatroid: FlagMatroid, -- the class of all flag matroids

Ways to use flagMatroid:
========================

  * "flagMatroid(List)"
  * "flagMatroid(Matrix,List)"

For the programmer
==================

