isWellDefined(KClass) -- whether the input is a well-defined equivariant K-class
********************************************************************************

  * Function: *note isWellDefined: (Macaulay2Doc)isWellDefined,
  * Usage: 
        isWellDefined C
  * Inputs:
      * C, an *note equivariant K-class: KClass,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, whether or not a list of
        Laurent polynomials satisfies edge compatibility condition

Description
===========

If $\{f_x \mid x\in X^T\}$ is a collection of Laurent polynomials in the
character ring $\mathbb Z[T_0, \ldots, T_n]$ of the torus $T$ acting on a *note
GKMVariety: GKMVariety, $X$, one per each torus-fixed point, representing an
element $C$ of $K_T^0(X^T)$, then $C$ is in the image of $K_T^0(X)$ under the
injective restriction map $K_T^0(X)\to K_T^0(X^T)$ if and only if it satisfies
the following "edge compatibility condition":

For each one-dimensional $T$-orbit-closure in $X$ with boundary points $x$ and
$x'$, one has $$f_x \equiv f_{x'} \ \mod \ 1 - T^{\lambda(x,x')}$$ where
$\lambda(x,x')$ is the character of the action of $T$ on the one-dimensional
orbit. See [Corollary 5.12; VV03] or [Corollary A.5; RK03] for details.



+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : PP3 = projectiveSpace 3                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = a "GKM variety" with an action of a 4-dimensional torus                 |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : GKMVariety                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : isWellDefined ampleKClass PP3 --the O(1) class on PP3 is well-defined   |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = true                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : badC = makeKClass(PP3, reverse gens PP3.characterRing) --reverse the    |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = an "equivariant K-class" on a GKM variety                               |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : KClass                                                                  |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|order of Laurent polynomials defining the O(1) class                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : isWellDefined badC --no longer well-defined                             |
|incompatible edges {{set {1}, set {3}}, {set {0}, set {1}}, {set {2}, set    |
|o4 = false                                                                   |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|{3}}, {set {0}, set {2}}}                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

A *note MomentGraph: MomentGraph, must be defined on the *note GKMVariety:
GKMVariety, on which the *note KClass: KClass, is a $K$-class of.



See also
========

  * *note KClass: KClass, -- the class of all equivariant K-classes
  * *note makeKClass: makeKClass, -- constructs an equivariant K-class

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note isWellDefined(KClass): isWellDefined_lpKClass_rp, -- whether the
    input is a well-defined equivariant K-class
