makeKClass(GKMVariety,FlagMatroid) -- the equivariant K-class of a flag matroid
*******************************************************************************

  * Function: *note makeKClass: makeKClass,
  * Usage: 
        C = makeKClass(X,FM)
  * Inputs:
      * X, a *note GKM variety: GKMVariety,, of *note lieType: lieType, "A"
        created by *note generalizedFlagVariety: generalizedFlagVariety,
      * FM, a *note flag matroid: FlagMatroid,, 
  * Outputs:
      * C, an *note equivariant K-class: KClass,, 

Description
===========

A flag matroid of whose constituent matroids have ranks $r_1, \ldots, r_k$ and
ground set size $n$ defines a *note KClass: KClass, on the (partial) flag
variety $Fl(r_1,\ldots, r_k;n)$.  When the flag matroid arises from a matrix
representing a point on the (partial) flag variety, this equivariant K-class
coincides with that of the structure sheaf of its torus orbit closure. See
[CDMS18] or [DES20].

+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : X = generalizedFlagVariety("A",2,{1,2})                  |
|                                                              |
|o1 = a "GKM variety" with an action of a 3-dimensional torus  |
|                                                              |
|o1 : GKMVariety                                               |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = matrix{{1,2,3},{0,2,3}}                              |
|                                                              |
|o2 = | 1 2 3 |                                                |
|     | 0 2 3 |                                                |
|                                                              |
|              2       3                                       |
|o2 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                        |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : FM = flagMatroid(A,{1,2})                                |
|                                                              |
|o3 = a "flag matroid" with rank sequence {1, 2} on 3 elements |
|                                                              |
|o3 : FlagMatroid                                              |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : C1 = makeKClass(X,FM)                                    |
|                                                              |
|o4 = an "equivariant K-class" on a GKM variety                |
|                                                              |
|o4 : KClass                                                   |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : C2 = orbitClosure(X,A)                                   |
|                                                              |
|o5 = an "equivariant K-class" on a GKM variety                |
|                                                              |
|o5 : KClass                                                   |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : C1 === C2                                                |
|                                                              |
|o6 = true                                                     |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note latticePoints(FlagMatroid): latticePoints_lpFlagMatroid_rp, --
    lattice points of a base polytope of a flag matroid
  * *note orbitClosure: orbitClosure, -- computes the equivariant K-class of a
    torus orbit closure of a point in a generalized flag variety
  * *note flagGeomTuttePolynomial: flagGeomTuttePolynomial, -- computes the
    flag-geometric Tutte polynomial of flag matroids

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note makeKClass(GKMVariety,FlagMatroid):
    makeKClass_lpGKMVariety_cmFlagMatroid_rp, -- the equivariant K-class of a
    flag matroid
