map(GKMVariety,GKMVariety,List) -- creates a EquivariantMap
***********************************************************

  * Function: *note map: (Macaulay2Doc)map,
  * Usage: 
        f = map(X,Y,L)
  * Inputs:
      * X, a *note GKM variety: GKMVariety,, the source GKM variety of the map
      * Y, a *note GKM variety: GKMVariety,, the target GKM variety of the map
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of pairs (x,y) where x and y are
        members of X.points and Y.points, respectively
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Degree: (Macaulay2Doc)map_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegree=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value null,
      * *note DegreeLift: (Macaulay2Doc)map_lpRing_cmRing_cmMatrix_rp, => ...,
        default value null,
      * *note DegreeMap: (Macaulay2Doc)map_lpRing_cmRing_cmMatrix_rp, => ...,
        default value null,
  * Outputs:
      * f, an *note equivariant map: EquivariantMap,, 

Description
===========

This method creates a *note EquivariantMap: EquivariantMap, given a GKM variety
$X$, a GKM variety $Y$, and a list L of pairs (x,y) where x and y are members
of X.points and Y.points (respectively), indicating that the torus-fixed point
x of X is sent to the torus-fixed point y of Y under the map.



The following describes the projection from the third Hizerbruch surface to the
projective line.



+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = makeCharacterRing 2;                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F3 = makeGKMVariety(hirzebruchSurface 3,R);                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : PP1 = projectiveSpace(1,R);                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : L = {({0,1},set {0}), ({0,3}, set{0}), ({1,2}, set{1}), ({2,3},         |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|set{1})};                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : f = map(F3,PP1,L)                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = an "equivariant map" of GKM varieties                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : EquivariantMap                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

This does not check that the morphism is well defined. In particular, it does
not verify that the map on torus-fixed points is induced by a morphism of GKM
varieties.

