setIndicator -- computes the signed indicator vector of an admissible set
*************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        setIndicator(T,n)
  * Inputs:
      * T, a *note set: (Macaulay2Doc)Set,, 
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, corresponding to a vector in
        $\mathbb Z^n$

Description
===========

Let $S$ be a set consisting of elements $s$, where $s$ is either equal to $i$
or $i^*$ with $0 \leq i \leq n-1$. The set $S$ is said to be admissible if for
any integer $i$, not both $i$ and $i^{*}$ are contained in $S$. This method
produces the signed indicator vector of $S$. In particular, the *note
setIndicator: setIndicator, of $S$ is $\sum c_ie_i \in \mathbb Z^n$ where $c_i
= 1$ if $i \in T$, $c_i = -1$ if $i^{*} \in T$ and $0$ otherwise.

+--------------------------+
|i1 : S1 = set{1,2,4,5};   |
+--------------------------+
|i2 : S2 = set{1,"2*"};    |
+--------------------------+
|i3 : setIndicator(S1,7)   |
|                          |
|o3 = {0, 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 0}|
|                          |
|o3 : List                 |
+--------------------------+
|i4 : setIndicator(S2,3)   |
|                          |
|o4 = {0, 1, -1}           |
|                          |
|o4 : List                 |
+--------------------------+

If the set is not admissible it produces an error.

+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S3 = set{1,"1*","2*",3}                              |
|                                                          |
|o1 = set {1, 1*, 2*, 3}                                   |
|                                                          |
|o1 : Set                                                  |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : setIndicator(S3,4)                                   |
|stdio:2:1:(3): error:  the signed subset is not admissible|
+----------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note generalizedFlagVariety: generalizedFlagVariety, -- makes a
    generalized flag variety as a GKM variety

